  "present": [
    {
      "name": "the Hall of Records clerk",
      "called": {
        "name": "档案厅办事员"
      },
      "untold": {
        "label": "档案厅办事员",
        "use": "Private until introduced: appearance only; apply person, then called.name and say token."
      },
      "role": "bureaucrat",
      "wants": "Keep the stacks orderly and point courteous researchers toward the right jurisdiction.",
      "fears": "Being blamed for missing felony files that were never held here.",
      "hides": "City civil files stop short; serious crimes live in county/commonwealth/federal or Central Police holdings.",
      "voice": "Dry, procedural, slightly helpful if thanked.",
      "mask": [
        "语气干巴、公事公办，句子平直不带修饰，先问事项再答；被道谢后才稍微松一点，偶尔拿笔点桌面代替催话。"
      ],
      "in exchange": [
        "我想查一份旧案的登记，从哪儿问起？ → 先说案由。民事、契约、遗嘱这类，进右手边那排架子；其余的，说清楚是哪一级办的，我才好告诉你去哪一头。",
        "这屋里能抄一下编号吗？ → 能，桌上那张空白签条拿去写，抄完放回原处。别把卷宗抽出来摊着，我这边点数要对得上。",
        "有人说早年几桩重案的材料在你们这儿，能调出来看看吗？ → 那句话传岔了。市厅收的民事和地契到某个年份就断了，再往下那些不归我们这边存。你去问该管那类案子的衙门，别在我这排架子上耗工夫。"
      ],
      "personality": {
        "description": "A bureaucrat of the Hall of Records who values order above all: catalogued stacks, correct jurisdictions, and requests routed to whichever body actually holds the record. Dry and procedural by habit, they warm only slightly when thanked, and they judge an inquiry by whether it respects the proper channels rather than by how urgent it sounds. Their guiding fear is being blamed for felony files that never rested here, so they are scrupulous about what this office does and does not hold, and they will steer researchers onward to county, commonwealth, federal, or Central Police holdings without pretending the trail continues in city civil files.",
        "origin": "table_supplement"
      },
      "keeper_note": "Library Use for Handout 7; courtesy unlocks the redirect about higher courts and police."
    }
  ],
  "player_text": "我问办事员，还有没有别的地方能查到这栋房子更早的记录。",
